    "title": "How to watch LSU women's basketball vs Duke in NCAA Tournament today",
    "text": "Updated March 27, 2026, 10:11 p.m. CTLSU women's basketball continues its March Madness run when it faces the Duke Blue Devils in a Friday night game. LSU took care of business last weekend, beating Jacksonville in the opening round before a dominant defensive performance against Texas Tech.If LSU wins, it would be the Tigers' fourth straight trip to the Elite Eight. The program has become a fixture in March under coach Kim Mulkey.LSU and Duke met in December, and the Tigers secured a 93-77 win on the road. But Duke turned it on after a rough stretch in nonconference play, and this Duke team isn't the same one LSU saw earlier this season.Watch LSU women's basketball vs. DukeThis will be the fifth time LSU and Duke have met in the NCAA Tournament since the turn of the century. LSU is 2-2 in those contests. The last tournament meeting was in 2010, when the Blue Devils beat LSU 60-52.Here's how to watch LSU-Duke women's basketball in the Sweet 16, including schedule, TV channel, streaming info and time.What channel is LSU women's basketball vs. Duke on today?TV Channel: ESPNLivestream:Fubo (free trial)LSU-Duke women's basketball will broadcast on ESPN. Streaming options for the game include Fubo, which offers a free trial to new subscribers.LSU women's basketball vs. Duke time todayDate: Friday, March 27Tipoff: 9 p.m. CTThe LSU-Duke women's basketball regional semifinal tips off at 9 p.m. CT from the Golden 1 Center in Sacramento, California.Watch LSU women's basketball vs. DukeLSU women's basketball vs. Duke PredictionLSU 75, Duke 68: Duke is a much better team than the last time LSU faced the Blue Devils. Kara Lawson's team will put up a fight, but I like LSU to get the job done and advance to the Elite Eight.NCAA women's basketball tournament -- Sweet 16 scheduleDayMatchupTime (ET)NetworkFriday, March 28(2) Vanderbilt vs. (6) Notre Dame2:30 p.m.ESPNFriday, March 28(1) UConn vs. (4) North Carolina5:00 p.m.ESPNFriday, March 28(1) UCLA vs. (4) Minnesota7:3